# haikuporter-scriptlet-build-tools.patch  (issue #136, porting-playbook Class 2)
#
# Patches haikuporter, not a recipe. Applied on the native arm64 builder by
# graviton/scripts/haiku-provision-native-builder (anchored, idempotent, verified)
# right after the haikuporter clone -- the native builder clones upstream
# haikuporter fresh, so a committed edit-in-place is how this fix reaches it (the
# same shape as haikuporter-cmake-policy-minimum.patch).
#
# WHY
# ---
# The #27 / Class-2 failure: a port shells out to a common build utility during
# BUILD()/INSTALL() but never declares it in BUILD_PREREQUIRES. haikuporter mounts
# ONLY a recipe's declared prerequisites -- plus a fixed base set -- into the
# build chroot, so the tool is absent even though the builder HOST has it
# installed, and the build dies `command not found` / `Error 127`. It was the
# largest auto-recoverable non-CMake class in the #136 backlog. Measured on the
# 20 Class-2 ports in the 2026-09-15/16 wave, the missing tool was one of these
# four universal utilities in 11 of them:
#
#     cmd:gzip   atari++, convmv, djvu, kakoune, libtermkey, mdate, unibilium
#                (7 -- almost always `gzip` compressing a man page on install)
#     cmd:tar    instead, mm_common   (2 -- install-time tar / configure probe)
#     cmd:unzip  betterspades         (1 -- unpacking a bundled archive)
#     cmd:which  autotrace            (1 -- autogen.sh pkg-config probe)
#
# Fixing this one recipe at a time (a `cmd:gzip` per-recipe overlay) is
# whack-a-mole, only reaches ports already touched, AND -- because a recipe
# overlay is baked into the AMI's ports tree -- needs a full rebake to take
# effect anyway. Proof it does not scale: atari++/autotrace/convmv/mdate/mm_common
# all had committed overlay recipes DECLARING the right cmd: tool, yet all failed
# again in the wave that ran after those overlays landed, because that wave's
# builder AMI predated them.
#
# THE SYSTEMIC FIX
# ----------------
# haikuporter has its own base prerequisite set:
# HaikuPorter/ShellScriptlets.py:scriptletPrerequirements is the list of commands
# it activates into EVERY chroot regardless of the recipe -- it already carries
# coreutils, cmd:bash, cmd:find, cmd:grep, cmd:sed, the objcopy/readelf/strip
# triplet, and cmd:xres. Appending the four universal build utilities there puts
# them in every build's chroot at once, via exactly the mechanism that already
# supplies sed/grep/coreutils. Those existing entries are themselves ports, so
# this introduces no new self-dependency class. scriptlet prerequisites are
# build-time only: they never become the built package's runtime REQUIRES.
#
# Scope is deliberately the four utilities any build/install step reasonably
# assumes are present -- the same "universal tool" bar the existing entries meet.
# Feature-specific tools stay per-recipe: gettext's msgfmt/msgattrib (an i18n port
# only -- blobwars, neverball) and dos2unix (a patch-time fixup -- hexcompare).
# Putting the 16 MB gettext package in every chroot would over-broaden.
#
# THE EDIT (HaikuPorter/ShellScriptlets.py, the scriptletPrerequirements literal):
#
#     scriptletPrerequirements = r'''
#     	coreutils
#     	cmd:bash
#     	cmd:find
#     	cmd:grep
#     	cmd:${targetMachinePrefix}objcopy
#     	cmd:${targetMachinePrefix}readelf
#     	cmd:sed
#     	cmd:${targetMachinePrefix}strip
#     	cmd:xres
#   + 	# graviton/DeBeOS (#136, Class 2): universal build utilities every recipe
#   + 	# reasonably assumes are present -- man-page gzip on `make install`, a
#   + 	# bundled-archive tar/unzip, a which-based configure probe -- but that
#   + 	# recipes routinely forget to declare. Same 'universal tool' bar as the
#   + 	# entries above (all of which are themselves ports), so no new
#   + 	# self-dependency class. Build-time only. Feature-specific tools
#   + 	# (gettext msgfmt/msgattrib, dos2unix) stay per-recipe.
#   + 	cmd:gzip
#   + 	cmd:tar
#   + 	cmd:unzip
#   + 	cmd:which
#     '''
#
# PROVIDER MAPPING (all confirmed present in the DeBeOS arm64 pool):
#   cmd:gzip   -> gzip     (app-arch/gzip;     gzip-1.14-1-arm64.hpkg)
#   cmd:tar    -> tar      (app-arch/tar;      tar-1.35-2-arm64.hpkg)
#   cmd:unzip  -> unzip    (app-arch/unzip;    unzip-6.10c23-6-arm64.hpkg)
#   cmd:which  -> which    (sys-apps/which;    which-2.21-6-arm64.hpkg)
# cmd:which resolvability is additionally confirmed by the wave logs: the
# nativebuild driver successfully `pkgman install`ed cmd:which for atari++ before
# it hit the (undeclared) gzip.
#
# Retire when: never as a class -- these are the coreutils-tier utilities a build
# is entitled to assume. An individual entry can be dropped only if it is added to
# Haiku's base image such that it is already present in a fresh chroot.
